Subject: [PATCH] mtk: dpmaif: defer traffic diagnostic dumps during CPU idle

The traffic_monitor callback prints queue and interface statistics, then
rearms its diagnostic timer. It does not service packets, refill buffers,
or enforce a hardware deadline. Mark only this timer TIMER_DEFERRABLE so
an idle CPU need not wake solely for a traffic dump.

The nominal interval and diagnostic callback remain unchanged. Dumps can
be delayed during idle; this is an explicit diagnostics tradeoff. Packet
IRQs, TX-completion timers, watchdogs, recovery and PM sequences remain
unchanged. This does not disable modem wakeups or alter radio firmware.

This targets the Rodin vendor CCCI module, not the common boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_com.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_com.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_com.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_dpmaif_com.c
@@ -3399,7 +3399,8 @@
 
 #if DPMAIF_TRAFFIC_MONITOR_INTERVAL
-	timer_setup(&dpmaif_ctl->traffic_monitor, dpmaif_traffic_monitor_func, 0);
+	timer_setup(&dpmaif_ctl->traffic_monitor, dpmaif_traffic_monitor_func,
+		    TIMER_DEFERRABLE);
 #endif
 	mtk_ccci_net_speed_init();
 
 	return 0;  /* dpmaif init succ. */
